 \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"4f5e913db23c0a315d77ace47590dcba0aad176e82d54d340fe6c1f7695f6be9","event_uuid":"dfaffe12-f279-496e-b76b-890adfd37508","position":{"commit_sha":"1506aa4e966a742ff5f71c15d7c8fd57e51a1389","position":"1788120016527468338-dfaffe12-f279-496e-b76b-890adfd37508"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"bdc4d76da7c6e569a68cbd4e4cef8f3c0322a883300143fb2a8785dbf1797772","event_uuid":"1655adf3-9709-4b9a-9fc3-9519c7be32f9","position":{"commit_sha":"7442a93c24b06779f1e1483a88bd1be41f05805e","position":"1788124750477453077-1655adf3-9709-4b9a-9fc3-9519c7be32f9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a78fdef9155740acfaf45e7fdb404a4218597be8b8201ac791186ded4711edca","event_uuid":"82cfef00-54aa-4902-9659-5dfd1ac87cfd","position":{"commit_sha":"c53d328d5a973e9c3ace0600fad3fab4b43d10f2","position":"1788125761468991034-82cfef00-54aa-4902-9659-5dfd1ac87cfd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1813e5987873be42265ef56794c607e7503af785bf34b2c150a781eee1f7bbb5","event_uuid":"9586bb1f-6af3-40f1-93c2-b7a599ef23a8","position":{"commit_sha":"a75b463a8fd0e35e0f1d3649545095dba912089b","position":"1788126173608943001-9586bb1f-6af3-40f1-93c2-b7a599ef23a8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"adb693808682c3b36d6ee51d03e2809044f1aca822e700cd9dafe4869ad7c643","event_uuid":"ba895601-690e-49db-a953-c4391ac72073","position":{"commit_sha":"05e687f1941cd6e2e0b731df44be5c5a8d26053b","position":"1788126198766677001-ba895601-690e-49db-a953-c4391ac72073"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788112361078681264,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a9145fbe-0e93-4eb4-84fc-59d6e440481b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"dc2c-0bb5-4272-46f3"},{"link_uuid":"1655adf3-9709-4b9a-9fc3-9519c7be32f9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1943-16f5-d4e8-4510"}],"description":"## Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/detectors.py:196` and\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:413` hardcode a `severity` string\n(`\"critical\"`, `\"high\"`) directly into a kernel-shaped finding without ever running through\n`pass3_decide` (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`), so these DET-tier findings carry no\ncomputed `validity`/`impact`/`priority`. The epic is migrating every consumer of `severity`\n(aggregation ranking, the review-bot comment, the `fail_on_severity` workflow gate) onto\n`priority` instead; DET-tier findings need a `priority` value before those consumers can\ntreat all findings uniformly. Both sites already carry `\"decision\": \"block\"` alongside\n`severity` -- only a `priority` value needs adding.\n\n`shim.py::_to_common_finding` (a downstream consumer NOT yet migrated to `priority` -- that\nmigration is a sibling ticket) reads `f.get(\"severity\")` off every blocking/advisory finding\nand maps it via `_KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY`, falling back to `_SEVERITY_DEFAULT = \"medium\"`\nwhen the key is absent. Deleting `severity` from these two DET findings NOW, before that\nconsumer migrates, would silently downgrade an always-block secrets/size-gate finding from\n`critical`/`high` to `medium` in the `review_result` shown to a human. This ticket therefore\nadds `priority` ALONGSIDE the existing `severity` (expand, not contract) -- the sibling\ncleanup ticket (byzantine-spinelike-penguin) removes `severity` last, once every consumer\n(this ticket's DET sites included) has something else to read.\n\n## Approach\nAt each hardcode site, ADD a `priority` float alongside the existing `severity` and\n`decision: \"block\"` keys (neither of which changes): the secrets detector's finding always\nblocks, so its priority is pinned above every configured `block_threshold` (`priority: 1.0`);\nthe bugfix-size-gate's finding is a strong-but-not-maximal signal (`priority: 0.9`). No key is\nremoved by this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `detectors.py`'s secrets-detector finding carries a new `priority: 1.0` key; its\n  existing `severity: \"critical\"` and `decision: \"block\"` keys are unchanged.\n- [x] `bugfix_size_gate.py`'s size-gate finding carries a new `priority: 0.9` key; its\n  existing `severity: \"high\"` and `decision: \"block\"` keys are unchanged.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py -k test_failclosed_forces_block_on_detector_match`\n  (the existing test at line 169, whose body asserts `severity`/`decision` at line 196) and\n  `pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py -k test_oversized_bug_fix_without_attestation_blocks`\n  (line 231, `decision` assertion at line 243) pass, with a new assertion added for the\n  `priority` key alongside each test's existing `severity`/`decision` assertions.\n- [x] `grep -c '\"priority\": 1.0' src/rebar/llm/code_review/detectors.py` and\n  `grep -c '\"priority\": 0.9' src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py` each print `1`\n  (verifying presence, not absence -- `severity` is intentionally retained by this ticket).\n\n## Testing\nTier: in-process unit test against the real detector/gate functions (pure calculation, no\nI/O). Oracle: the returned finding dict carries both the new `priority` value and the\nunchanged `severity`/`decision` values, asserted exactly. The RED oracles to strengthen are\n`test_failclosed_forces_block_on_detector_match` (test_code_review_ws5.py:169, asserting\n`severity`/`decision` at line 196) and\n`test_oversized_bug_fix_without_attestation_blocks`\n(test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:231, asserting `decision` at line 243) -- add a `priority`\nassertion to each; keep the existing `severity`/`decision` assertions passing as a\nregression check that expand-contract left them intact.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/detectors.py","reason":"secrets-detector finding gets a fixed priority/decision instead of hardcoded severity"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py","reason":"size-gate finding gets a fixed priority/decision instead of hardcoded severity"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_detectors.py","reason":"update assertions for priority/decision keys"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","dc2c-0bb5-4272-46f3"],["parent","c4c8-317a-85ca-4b08"],["relates_to","1943-16f5-d4e8-4510"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"c4c8-317a-85ca-4b08","parent_status_uuid":"9586bb1f-6af3-40f1-93c2-b7a599ef23a8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e0d5-2b29-2814-4421","ticket_type":"task","title":"Assign fixed priority to DET-tier findings (secrets detector, bugfix-size gate)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ff7ea208-ca81-4851-93e5-86c7691955bf","a4ec18d8-87ca-4d02-97c4-9027784b77a5","dc4a82d2-30a7-423f-acd4-0ad80a221ea8","a86322f